WEBVTT

00:02:56.339 --> 00:03:00.551
go to somewhere completely different,
talk to other fish,

00:03:00.593 --> 00:03:02.637
and then look back at ourselves

00:03:02.637 --> 00:03:06.098
to try and understand
the assumptions that shape us.

00:03:06.974 --> 00:03:11.520
In my case, I did that
by going to Soviet Tajikistan.

00:03:11.812 --> 00:03:16.067
But later on, I used that perspective
of jumping out of my fishbowl

00:03:16.108 --> 00:03:18.694
to look back at my own world,

00:03:18.736 --> 00:03:21.113
where I now work as a journalist,

00:03:21.113 --> 00:03:24.283
to look at the world of finance,
to look at the world of business,

00:03:24.283 --> 00:03:26.535
to try and look at it with fresh eyes

00:03:26.577 --> 00:03:30.039
and to see not just the parts
of the world that are obvious